---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy vs Terms of Service: Key Differences"
  description="Understand the difference between privacy policies and terms of service. Learn what each document covers and why you need both."
  keywords="privacy policy vs terms of service, terms and conditions, legal documents, website legal pages"
>
  <section class="article-page">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <a href="/privacy-basics">Privacy Basics</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span>Privacy Policy vs Terms</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="article-header">
        <h1>Privacy Policy vs <span class="gradient-text">Terms of Service</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">Understanding the key differences between these two essential legal documents.</p>
        <div class="meta">
          <span>8 min read</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>Updated April 2026</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="content-wrapper">
        <article class="article-content">
          <section>
            <h2>What Is a Privacy Policy?</h2>
            <p>A <strong>privacy policy</strong> focuses exclusively on how a company collects, uses, stores, and shares your personal information. It's about <em>your data</em> and your rights over it.</p>
            <p>Key topics covered:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>What personal information is collected</li>
              <li>How data is used and processed</li>
              <li>Third-party data sharing</li>
              <li>Cookie and tracking technologies</li>
              <li>Data retention periods</li>
              <li>Your privacy rights (access, deletion, etc.)</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>What Are Terms of Service?</h2>
            <p><strong>Terms of Service</strong> (also called Terms and Conditions) govern the overall relationship between you and the company. They cover rules, obligations, and legal limitations.</p>
            <p>Key topics covered:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>User eligibility and account rules</li>
              <li>Acceptable use policies</li>
              <li>Intellectual property rights</li>
              <li>Liability limitations</li>
              <li>Dispute resolution procedures</li>
              <li>Account suspension/termination</li>
              <li>Governing law and jurisdiction</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Key Differences at a Glance</h2>
            <div class="comparison-grid">
              <div class="compare-col">
                <h3>Privacy Policy</h3>
                <ul>
                  <li>Focus: <strong>Your data</strong></li>
                  <li>Purpose: Transparency</li>
                  <li>Driven by: Privacy laws</li>
                  <li>Your benefit: Know your rights</li>
                  <li>Updates: When data practices change</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="compare-col">
                <h3>Terms of Service</h3>
                <ul>
                  <li>Focus: <strong>The service</strong></li>
                  <li>Purpose: Rules and obligations</li>
                  <li>Driven by: Business needs</li>
                  <li>Your benefit: Know the rules</li>
                  <li>Updates:随时通知</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Which One Should You Read?</h2>
            <p><strong>Read both!</strong> But here's when each matters:</p>
            
            <h3>Read the Privacy Policy When:</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>You're concerned about data privacy</li>
              <li>You want to know what info is collected</li>
              <li>You're evaluating a service's privacy practices</li>
              <li>You want to exercise your data rights</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Read the Terms of Service When:</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>You're signing up for a new service</li>
              <li>You need to understand your obligations</li>
              <li>You're concerned about liability</li>
              <li>You want to know how disputes are handled</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Why Both Matter</h2>
            <p>While they serve different purposes, both documents are legally binding. By using a service, you're agreeing to both.</p>
            <p>Companies must provide both under various laws. The privacy policy is often more regulated due to privacy laws like GDPR and CCPA.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="cta-box">
            <h2>Analyze Any Legal Document</h2>
            <p>Use PolicyLens to understand both privacy policies and terms of service in plain language.</p>
            <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Try PolicyLens Free</a>
          </section>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .article-page { padding: 40px 0 80px; }
  .container { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
  .breadcrumbs { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 32px; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .breadcrumbs a { color: var(--accent-cyan); }
  .article-header { margin-bottom: 48px; text-align: center; }
  .article-header h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .meta { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 12px; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .article-content h2 { font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 48px 0 24px; padding-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); }
  .article-content h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; padding-top: 0; border: none; }
  .article-content h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 32px 0 16px; }
  .article-content p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .article-content ul { color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 16px 0 24px 24px; }
  .article-content li { margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: 1.7; }
  .comparison-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 24px; margin: 24px 0; }
  .compare-col { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 24px; }
  .compare-col h3 { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .compare-col ul { margin: 0; list-style: none; }
  .compare-col li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05); }
  .cta-box { background: var(--bg-secondary); border-radius: var(--radius-xl); padding: 40px; text-align: center; margin-top: 48px; }
  .cta-box h2 { border: none; margin: 0 0 12px; padding: 0; }
  .cta-box p { margin-bottom: 24px; }
  @media (max-width: 768px) { .comparison-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
